# REA Research Lab: ten studies of released software

A reproducible collection of ten bounded reverse-engineering projects, prepared for Ginderlax on 12 October 2026. Each combines identified release bytes, actual Reverse Engineer Anything (REA) observations, a reconstructed contract, comparisons with the original software, and a research report.

Start with [the series manuscript](SERIES-STUDY.md), [methods and evidence standards](METHODOLOGY.md), or an individual report below. The studies demonstrate specific mechanisms; they do not claim reconstruction of entire products or hosted services. They are documented engineering studies and have not undergone independent academic peer review.

## Product development

[REA Studio](products/rea-studio/README.md) adds ten runnable local development applications with a shared interface, persisted data and integration tests. The user's completion standard is every documented feature of the original products, plus improvements in speed, resource use, ease of use, compatibility and reliability. **Zero complete replacement products meet that standard yet.** The [acceptance requirements](products/rea-studio/ACCEPTANCE.md), [status record](products/rea-studio/STATUS.json) and individual application READMEs preserve the full scope and identify missing capabilities. Recorded component comparisons include tradeoffs as well as improvements.

The historical [native exchange and source control milestone](products/rea-studio/NATIVE-EXCHANGE-MILESTONE.md) added supported KeePass KDBX, Joplin JEX and Excalidraw scene exchange, editor Git controls and exact sequence differences, with 112 passing tests. The historical [dashboard, execution and archive milestone](products/rea-studio/EXECUTION-ARCHIVE-MILESTONE.md) added native Grafana dashboard editing, HTTP workflows with cancellation, ZIP64/TAR/GZIP support and editor optimization, with 176 passing tests. The historical [native workflow milestone](products/rea-studio/NATIVE-WORKFLOWS-MILESTONE.md) records 345 passing checks. The historical [compression and remote synchronization milestone](products/rea-studio/COMPRESSION-REMOTE-MILESTONE.md) preserves the 496-test checkpoint. The historical [Rabin, workflow routing and drawing geometry milestone](products/rea-studio/RABIN-ROUTING-GEOMETRY-MILESTONE.md) preserves the 607-test checkpoint. The historical [packed backups, notebook organization and Vault history milestone](products/rea-studio/PACKS-NOTEBOOKS-HISTORY-MILESTONE.md) adds native data-pack aggregation, notebook tree editing/note moves and native history restore with pending-draft corrections, with **686 passing implemented-contract checks and 0 skips**. It retains source-bound original comparisons, actual browser evidence, failure histories and three unaccepted Metrics experiments. Full-product requirements and measured regressions stay explicit; the development goal remains active.

The latest hosted full-suite repeat, [run `38933603615`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38933603615) on the metadata-only branch revision `089cb234`, passes **1,100/1,100 checks with zero failures or skips**. Its complete 431-file local evidence backup is readable. The immediately preceding [D24 full-suite failure](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full1100-native-metadata-failure-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) remains unresolved: run `38932318510` passed **1,098 of 1,100 checks** and failed two Archive creation groups when native Windows source metadata was unavailable or invalid. Both failed groups took about 15.6–15.8 seconds against a 15-second native-child limit, but the original transport error was redacted, so a timeout is an inference, not an observed cause. A separate hosted diagnostic is being prepared with the same runtime deadline and assertions. The newer pass neither diagnoses nor erases the failed attempt; its exact ZIP, raw output and all 431 uploaded files remain recoverable. Earlier 1,100-pass epochs retain their original source scope.

Committed Notes task editing separately passes **92/92 groups and eight browser scenarios** on its recorded 32-file source epoch. The New To-do **111/111 and eight-scenario** result below remains an experiment; its 36-file source is not installed. Current publication verification passes all **208 controls, both root phases and 963 syntax checks**, with 92 readable artifact files and 56 authenticated Notes-envelope sources. The exact two derived metadata files were imported at `089cb234`; its automatic repeat confirms the same canonical payload and manifest. These later preservation and documentation changes need fresh publication validation. Complete-product parity and superiority remain unproven.

The separately composed [New To-do experiment](products/rea-studio/results/notes-new-todo-r5-cloud-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) now passes **111/111 selected checks and eight real Chromium scenarios** in run `38930449217`, on source `89e00f6`. It adds a direct task draft and first-save flow, including duplicate-save prevention, newer-draft retention and genuine refresh-failure recovery. All 1,108 uploaded files are recoverable from two complete public ZIPs and readable local backups. The earlier four finite failures and one browser failure remain documented with exact sources; the correction keeps every older check. This is accepted experimental evidence. Installing the 36-file candidate into the normal Notes application requires a separate source-proof transition and fresh installed checks. The installed 32-file application and its 92/8 evidence remain unchanged; counts are never added together.

| Project | Released component and valuable mechanism | Recorded comparison unit | Report |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 01 · VS Code / Monaco | Monaco 0.57.0 sequence-diff kernel | 5,002 exact outputs; 5,002 separate replay checks | [Study](projects/01-vscode-monaco/REPORT.md) |
| 02 · Grafana | @grafana/data 13.2.3 telemetry reduction | 20,720 result objects, each with 19 fields | [Study](projects/02-grafana/REPORT.md) |
| 03 · n8n | n8n-workflow 2.16.0 extraction graph utilities | 40,611 method results; 4,609 specifically validate extraction selections | [Study](projects/03-n8n/REPORT.md) |
| 04 · Excalidraw | 0.18.1 camera transforms and scene-version values | 4,004 original comparisons; 1,500 separate model invariants | [Study](projects/04-excalidraw/REPORT.md) |
| 05 · Joplin | Renderer 3.7.1 links and heading anchors | 1,630 recognition, parsing, decoding and heading comparisons | [Study](projects/05-joplin/REPORT.md) |
| 06 · Node-RED | Nodes 5.0.8 Switch routing | 924 output-port/error comparisons | [Study](projects/06-node-red/REPORT.md) |
| 07 · KeePass | 2.61.1 HOTP/TOTP component | 485 original assembly results | [Study](projects/07-keepass/REPORT.md) |
| 08 · 7-Zip | Extra 26.04 x64 DLL property export | 400 rows, 255 unique inputs; 11 separate model-only signature checks | [Study](projects/08-7zip/REPORT.md) |
| 09 · restic | v0.19.1 small-file addressing and identity across snapshots | 122 content-ID lists; additional identity/integrity checks separately recorded | [Study](projects/09-restic/REPORT.md) |
| 10 · rclone | v1.75.2 synthetic obfuscation format | 230 assertions on 115 original CLI outputs; 115 separate length checks | [Study](projects/10-rclone/REPORT.md) |

Every final recorded differential comparison passes in its declared corpus. Counts use different units, include repeated and calibrated cases, and should not be summed into a statistical performance score. Some initial hypotheses failed and were corrected; the reports retain those histories. Monaco also exposes a reduced witness where the original kernel produces a nonminimal edit script, despite our exact compatibility with its output.

## Inspect or reproduce

The reports, study metadata, claim ledgers, code and synthetic observations are readable without installing REA. Run `node scripts/verify-records.mjs` to check the publication hashes, required records and JavaScript syntax. To repeat an experiment, use the documented wrapper commands in its report. Those wrappers preserve historical results in new ignored replay directories. Some retained low-level native verification scripts write existing evidence paths; the native reports identify these scripts.

Projects 01–06 need Node.js. Original-artifact execution in projects 07–10 uses the recorded Windows x64 environment; the native projects also use Python and Windows PowerShell. Artifact acquisition and analysis engines are separate from experiment execution. [TOOLING.md](TOOLING.md) explains the two REA runtimes and optional provider requirements.

## Preservation and publication

The local collection retains original distributables, full evidence, dependency files, engine installations and replay repositories under ignored `artifacts/`, `node_modules/` and `tooling/` directories. The public [Ginderlax/rea-research-lab repository](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab) stores research reports, reconstructed code, harnesses, acquisition digests, selected evidence and recorded observations. GitHub is not an archival mirror of every vendor distributable; those exact originals remain on the local machine.

The separate `rea-backup-2026-10-12` backup was preserved unchanged. [PUBLICATION-MANIFEST.json](PUBLICATION-MANIFEST.json) hashes the research payload. The local publication receipt records the verified remote commit. [License scope and attribution](LICENSES.md) explain why no blanket license is applied to the collection.

## Developer feedback

We welcome independent reproduction, small counterexamples, corrections to the reports, and suggestions for stronger REA experiments. [Open a research feedback issue](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/issues/new?template=research-feedback.md) or submit a pull request. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) explains how to make a result easy to reproduce and review.

For REA Studio, [report an application defect or missing feature](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/issues/new?template=product-feedback.md). Include an exact revision, synthetic steps and the original release/documentation when making a compatibility claim.

Useful starting points include Monaco's nonminimal edit-script witness, Grafana's counter-reset behavior, n8n's edge-selection rules, KeePass's boundary cases, and the limits of REA's partial semantic traces. Findings should identify the exact component and release; the collection's scope is ten bounded mechanisms rather than ten complete product replicas.

The historical [search, Save, notebook trash and entry recycling checkpoint](products/rea-studio/SEARCH-TRASH-RECYCLE-SAVE-MILESTONE.md) passes **811 implemented-contract checks, zero skips, and709 source fingerprints stable**. It preserves confirmed failures and independent corrections,138 focused Notes/Vault checks and78 Editor checks, an incomplete native-confirmation browser attempt, the acquired VS Code1.140.0 release and its finite API declaration inventory, and four unaccepted Metrics campaigns. Full replacement and all comparative acceptance gates remain open.

[Prior source-bound Editor browser acceptance](products/rea-studio/results/editor-current-search-save-browser-20261013/frozen/validation.json.snapshot) passes eight finite groups, including three delayed responses after real disk commits, with31 exact named source identities from before the later Sketch host-route insertion and normal owned cleanup. These checks add browser evidence for search and Save; full feature parity and comparative acceptance remain open.

The historical [notebook confirmation, drawing layout and editor value API checkpoint](products/rea-studio/NOTES-LAYOUT-VALUE-API-MILESTONE.md) passes **847 implemented-contract checks,0skips and720stable source fingerprints**. Notes passes69focused checks and8browser groups; Sketch39app/2HTTP checks and14browser groups; Editor API13pure checks. Source snapshots, confirmed failures, strictness/precision corrections, independent review and exact historical host transitions remain inspectable. Zero products satisfy the accepted complete replacement and comparative standard.

The last published [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint](products/rea-studio/EDITOR-PATTERN-VAULT-GROUP-MILESTONE.md) passes **937 implemented-contract checks, no skips and 737 stable source fingerprints**. It adds bounded pattern search, corrected native textarea navigation and recursive Vault group recovery. Exact sources, independent negative reviews, original comparisons and finite browser limits are preserved. Full replacements and comparative acceptance remain under development.

On 15 October 2026, development resumed after an interrupted verification run. That attempt remains incomplete; the later hosted Flow/Vault result below provides separate finite acceptance. The 937-test checkpoint above retains its historical source epoch. [Cloud verification and recoverable evidence](CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) describes the hosted Windows process. The current implemented full suite subsequently passed as recorded below; full replacements and comparative acceptance remain pending.

The earlier [hosted Flow/Vault recovery run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passed **282/282 finite contract checks with zero skips** on revision `14e4859`, with a stable 762-file census and 340 preserved active source snapshots. That record remains a separate source epoch.

The [later Flow/Vault and collector-control run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-controls-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **282/282 finite contract checks with zero skips** on revision `a2e0aa7`, with a stable 764-file census and 342 active source snapshots in the verified complete local backup. All four synthetic collector controls pass separately. Its public capsule preserves receipts, raw logs and control evidence; 342 application and 60 synthetic source-snapshot payloads remain in the local backup, with their identities and manifests retained publicly. The [first Archive attempt](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-composition-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) failed baseline-census qualification before acquisition or tests and remains a separate failed epoch.

The earlier [Archive experimental run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-metadata-failure-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) executed **160 checks: 154 passed and six failed**, with zero skips, on the composed overlay based on revision `9970992`. Its 776-file census stayed stable; 354 active source snapshots remain in the complete local backup, while metadata, raw logs and observations are preserved publicly. This remains a separate failed epoch.

The earlier [Archive and prerequisite run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-prerequisites-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) executed **161 checks: 155 passed and six failed**, with zero skips, on the overlay based on `b15d166`; its 779-file census stayed stable and 357 source snapshots are backed up locally. Acquisition of the pinned bsdtar EXE/DLL pair and other development inputs succeeded, and one separate original `--version` smoke passed. This failed source epoch remains preserved.

The [later Archive finite experiment](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **161/161 checks with zero failures or skips** after the literal-path correction. Run `38808918976` tested the composed overlay on actual Git merge `7d5bde3`, distinct from PR head `aeb62e6`; its 779-file census remained stable. The path diagnostics confirm real short-name/long-name aliases while the metadata checks pass. All 389 evidence files, including 357 source snapshots, remain in the verified local backup; the public capsule retains all non-source evidence and the omitted snapshots' identities. Original prerequisites, the separate one-process bsdtar smoke and the post-run source check also passed. Production installation remains false; browser acceptance, the full Archive scope and the full ten-application suite remain pending.

The [first full hosted replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full-suite-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) completed 1,042 current checks: 1,024 passed and 18 failed, with zero skips. Actual tested merge `abcac0b2` plus the explicit three-file oracle-test overlay retained a stable 770-file census. One Editor observer compares different spellings of the same Windows root; 17 WebDAV checks fail at the current workspace-alias restriction. The failed raw output and all metadata are preserved publicly, and all 348 active snapshots remain in the verified local backup. The later focused experiment below verifies candidate Windows corrections; the exact reviewed sources were subsequently integrated; fresh hosted full-suite validation subsequently passed as recorded below. This is a failed full-suite record, with no replacement or superiority acceptance.

The [focused Windows path experiment](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-windows-path-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **47/47 finite Editor Git and Sync WebDAV checks with zero skips** on actual tested merge `93b5dbe7`, separate from PR head `b0cdb550`. It uses an explicit three-target derivative: one Sync runtime correction, one Editor path-observer correction and one new regression file. A genuine hosted Windows short-root alias was observed; the 772-file composed census and separate three-target postcheck stayed exact. All 350 active source snapshots remain in the verified complete local backup. The exact three reviewed sources were subsequently [installed in the local application source](products/rea-studio/results/windows-path-installed-20261015/installation-receipt.json), with verified before/after bytes. The subsequent [hosted committed-source check](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-windows-path-installed-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes 47/47 with zero skips on merge `4a69ae1f`, authenticates all 350 eligible active sources against Git and passes the separate source postcheck. The fresh implemented full-suite pass is recorded below; the failed 1,042-check record is unchanged.

The [hosted Flow/Vault browser run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-browser-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **12/12 finite Chromium cases**, with zero failures, skips or retries, on unmodified tested merge `f138ee5a`, separate from PR head `dc0fce2b`. It verifies three real downloads byte for byte and records twelve screenshots, six real-response timing holds and two explicitly programmatic probes of disabled Flow controls; the latter are not ordinary user typing. All 326 captured source identities stayed exact and their snapshots remain in the verified complete local backup. The public capsule retains every non-source artifact file, the raw downloads and viewable PNG evidence. No original product runs occurred. These results do not establish Archive browser, full-suite, browser-matrix, full-product or comparative acceptance; counts from different campaigns are not added.

The [integrated full-suite replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full-suite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **1,048/1,048 implemented checks with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos** in run `38816488464` on actual merge `4a69ae1f8e0156fa9608faf357d415f536ba95f7`, separate from PR head `464be289`. It includes the committed Windows correction and an explicitly composed three-source paired-bsdtar test-loader overlay. Application runtime sources match Git; all 773 census identities stayed stable, all prerequisites passed, and the independent source postcheck passed. The complete portable evidence and 351 active source snapshots are verified in the local backup. The public capsule retains every non-source-tree artifact file and the omitted source identities. This result covers the current implemented suite; every documented original feature and the requested whole-product quality comparisons remain open. The historical 937/737 and failed 1,042/18 records remain unchanged.
