 ## Latest verified follow-up
 
+The latest completed full-suite repeat is [run `38933603615`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38933603615): **1,100/1,100 checks pass**, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos, on actual tested merge `ca0de9212406f69dd46f87e499025bb0f001f4a6` for metadata-only branch head `089cb2341cea6519a2bbb11f2c6588131f6e67bd`. All 798 census identities remain stable and all 374 active snapshots are retained in its complete 431-file readable local backup. Artifact `12061336112` is 1,726,276 bytes with SHA256 `8aa4c41f307d77347a015f78a6f7beab29361bb75b6c973b91e87ffe93627947`. This is a separate repeat, not a replacement for any earlier receipt.
+
+The immediately preceding [D24 full-suite attempt](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full1100-native-metadata-failure-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) remains a confirmed, unresolved failure: [run `38932318510`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38932318510) executes **1,100 checks: 1,098 pass and two fail**, with no skips, on actual merge `5f23f782a7224aaacdce89edfe21eb7e3a565831` for branch head `d24db806`. The two Archive creation groups refuse native Windows source metadata; their 15,798.2349 ms and 15,590.5217 ms durations align with the 15,000 ms native-child limit. The adapter discarded the original child error and redacted the transport/parse reason, so a timeout is not established. All 798 census bytes and 374 source snapshots match the separately successful `89e00f6` full run byte for byte. Five prerequisite receipts and the independent oracle postcheck passed. Its complete exact public ZIP preserves all 431 uploaded files, both failed TAP blocks and all native metadata sources; 57 nonsource artifact roles are also directly retained. The newer 089c pass does not identify the cause or erase these failures. A separate hosted diagnostic is being prepared to record the native transport outcome under the unchanged command, deadline and test assertions. No runtime correction or reliability acceptance is claimed.
+
+Publication on D24 [run `38932318654`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38932318654) and metadata-only 089c [run `38933603624`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38933603624) passes **208 controls, both root phases and 963 syntax checks**. Both retain 92 readable artifact files plus all 56 decoded Notes-envelope sources. The assessed payload has 28,806 files and 1,364,428,861 bytes; its canonical row identity and publication manifest are equal across the metadata-only transition. Only the two authenticated derived metadata paths were imported at `089cb234`; the automatic repeat's new observation clocks do not require another import. The new failure capsule, diagnostic sources and this documentation form a later payload that requires fresh publication verification. Publication controls execute no application tests and establish no feature or comparative acceptance.
+
+The earlier installed-Notes, Archive and full-suite records below retain their exact source epochs. New To-do's separately accepted 111/8 experimental result is still uninstalled; it is not added to the installed 92 groups, eight browser cases or full-suite total.
+
 The reviewed **Notes task-editing sources are installed and pass fresh committed-source checks**. The [finite job](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-installed-finite-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **92/92 groups across 17 fixed files**, including 23 new groups, and separately records 20 released Joplin helper comparisons. The [browser job](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-installed-browser-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **8/8 real Chromium cases**, with four genuine successful-response holds, two byte-exact downloads, eight screenshots and complete owned cleanups, and one actual HTTP 400 conflict followed by explicit retry. Run `38917424088` tests committed `362bda055ac4cf7201b2d6a75a2b30dc6fedb578` with zero source overlays. Both jobs authenticate all 32 Notes files, eight after-image pins and 27 dependencies before and after execution; independent postchecks pass. Complete 449-file and 495-file local backups are readable, and their exact public portable ZIPs retain every uploaded role. The first readback-tool CRLF extraction failure and both reader versions remain preserved; no product rerun was needed. Native JEX readback retains six unchanged serialized records and the exact binary resource. No original full application or GUI execution is claimed. The [actual installation journal](products/rea-studio/results/notes-todo-installed-20261016/installation-receipt.json) retains its then-pending acceptance wording and all source recovery pins; older experimental results remain separate. The broader implemented suite now passes as recorded below; the successful 208-control publication result is recorded below.
 
-The [fresh full implemented-suite run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-installed-full1100-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **1,100/1,100 groups with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos** in [run `38917433182`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38917433182), testing actual merge `6c3c4ecad2c60c55eddd8909c0c8d46acf647137` for branch head `362bda05`. All 796 census identities remain stable; 369 eligible committed sources match Git, with exactly three explicit Archive oracle-test loader/helper targets composed. Application runtime and Notes sources have no overlays. All seven eligible Notes after-images, all 17 Notes test files, the 23 authored task groups and 20 separately counted released-helper comparisons are authenticated within this run. The Notes README is outside this verifier's eligible source census; the focused installed jobs authenticate it separately. All five same-attempt prerequisite receipts and the separate oracle-source postcheck pass. The complete 429-file local backup is readable; its exact public outer ZIP retains all 372 source snapshots and every other uploaded byte, while all 57 nonsource roles are also directly retained. The separate 92 finite groups, eight browser cases, 161 Archive groups and overlapping three bounds groups are never added to 1,100. This verifies implemented contracts; every documented feature and whole-product superiority remain unproven.
