-The [fresh publication replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-publication-208-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **all 208 controls, both root validation phases and 959 syntax checks** in [run `38922041634`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38922041634), testing actual merge `fee4a29bf635d42f54fa069bd0aa1268fcb7ff8a` for branch head `25b54d7`. The **28,386-file / 1,342,588,854-byte** assessed payload remains stable; only the two derived metadata paths change. The generated publication manifest is validated. Complete 92-file local evidence and the 56-source Notes envelope are readable and authenticated; the exact public outer ZIP retains every uploaded byte. All 208 control rows, both raw root output pairs, raw API/logs and source/reader context remain preserved. An independent audit matches the envelope source bytes to the actual tested Git tree. This resolves the two earlier publication failures while retaining their original records, all control groups and read limits. Publication verification executes no application tests or original products and adds no behavioral or parity claim. These preservation objects and documentation add a later payload, which requires its own hosted validation before only its two derived metadata files may be imported.
+The [earlier 959-syntax publication replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-publication-208-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **all 208 controls, both root validation phases and 959 syntax checks** in [run `38922041634`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38922041634), testing actual merge `fee4a29bf635d42f54fa069bd0aa1268fcb7ff8a` for branch head `25b54d7`. The **28,386-file / 1,342,588,854-byte** assessed payload remains stable; only the two derived metadata paths change. The generated publication manifest is validated. Complete 92-file local evidence and the 56-source Notes envelope are readable and authenticated; the exact public outer ZIP retains every uploaded byte. All 208 control rows, both raw root output pairs, raw API/logs and source/reader context remain preserved. An independent audit matches the envelope source bytes to the actual tested Git tree. This resolves the two earlier publication failures while retaining their original records, all control groups and read limits. Publication verification executes no application tests or original products and adds no behavioral or parity claim. These preservation objects and documentation add a later payload, which requires its own hosted validation before only its two derived metadata files may be imported.
 
 The [subsequent publication attempt and retained-control correction](products/rea-studio/results/followup-control-four-epochs-correction-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) preserve all 85 files, the complete outer ZIP and all 56 decoded Notes source-envelope payloads from run `38920820160` at branch `c15dd78` and tested merge `e77bb17e`. The corrected ID assertions pass; **121 controls pass before control 122 fails**, with zero root phases started. One older positive control still expects no historical route for the earlier followup reader, contradicting the exact Notes route already checked successfully in the same run. The correction requires that exact preserved before-image, adds an explicit current-reader identity assertion inside the same group, and retains all 208 groups, older mappings, unknown-identity rejections and read limits. The migration resolver, producer and application sources are unchanged. Independent source and complete-backup review passes; fresh hosted replay remains required.
 
