const document=`# Flow static links and Vault group editing checkpoint\n\nFlow now edits and executes supported native Node-RED static Link In/Out graphs while preserving unedited source text. Vault creates and edits native KeePass groups, preserving unknown XML and guarding drafts entered during delayed refreshes. These are installed capabilities in the continuing ten-product program. **Zero products meet the requested complete replacement and comparative acceptance standard.**\n\n## Current installed run\n\nThe fresh suite passes **${total}/${total} implemented-contract checks**, with no failures, cancellations, skips or unfinished tests. All **${sources} eligible source files** were captured before execution and stayed exact afterwards. The run took ${attempt.summary.duration_ms} ms on Node 24.16.0. [Raw output and exact sources](${prefix}/preservation-manifest.json), [development receipt](results/development-validation.json) and [reviewed installation](${installationPath}) bind this epoch. The installation changes35 app paths (9 replacements,26 additions) and one exact source-only historical proof module; it keeps731 of the previous737 eligible code/data sources unchanged.\n\n| Application | Installed behavior | Remaining boundaries |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Flow | Static Link In/Out unions, Connect/Disconnect, saved/deployed separation, native raw-source Save/Export, guarded import and retained execution history. | Link Call/return, subflows, wider node ecosystem, scheduler/network behavior and complete Node-RED workflows. |\n| Vault | Native group IDs, bounded Create/Save names and notes, inherited settings, encrypted persistence, rollback and newer-draft guards. | Broader group settings/moves, whole-bin commands, providers/plugins, original GUI and complete database compatibility. |\n\n[Static link contracts](apps/flow/NATIVE-LINKS.md), [native text behavior](apps/flow/NATIVE-TEXT-SOURCE.md) and [group editing](apps/vault/GROUP-EDIT.md) give runnable steps, resource limits and source notices. Selected official Node-RED sources retain Apache notices; KeePass sources and derived assistance retain GPL notices.\n\n## Independent failures and bounded acceptance\n\nFlow preserves its initial static-link author epoch, model corrections, a real-browser CRLF false-dirty failure, a separate raw-source correction and independent review. The corrected author campaign passes75 groups;24 independent model groups include14 replays plus10 fresh cases. Twelve ordinary shared-host browser observations pass, including three actual1812-byte native downloads matching the same raw seed, one native file-chooser import and four manual Inject runs. Browser held-response, bare-CR and pending-disposal acceptance were not performed. Counts overlap and are never added to the combined suite. [Flow complete source map](apps/flow/results/native-link-textarea-followup/plan/public-source-map.json.snapshot) retains six exact epochs, the failed attempts, original compiler/runtime comparisons and license sources.\n\nVault preserves the885 author stage, the independent78-artifact negative review, the137 correction,55 corrected independent artifacts and separate HTTP and browser epochs. Two independently reproduced Create/Save defects lost a newer name/notes draft after a delayed final roster refresh; the correction validates generation and draft state after that refresh. Fifteen corrected independent model groups cover persistence, retries and disposal. Nine ordinary native-browser observations pass for literal names/notes, subsequent native-ID Save, dirty close/discard, parent rename, entry/group draft protection and reload. Held native-browser transport acceptance and original full GUI execution remain unperformed. [Vault complete source map](apps/vault/results/group-edit-followup/plan/source-proof/preservation-manifest.json.snapshot) preserves1230 logical aliases (832 existing reuse,398 new aliases represented by234 distinct new payloads) and59 explicit private/generated exclusions.\n\nIndependent installation review caught a Windows absolute-path import and an overly broad source-path restriction before execution. The corrected installer uses a file URL and exactly11 hash-bound canonical snapshots for approved synthetic source records; public/live paths retain their private-path ban. Negative and corrected reviews remain inspectable.\n\n## Historical evidence and ongoing work\n\nThe previous [937-check checkpoint](EDITOR-PATTERN-VAULT-GROUP-MILESTONE.md) retains737 exact source identities; the earlier [847-check checkpoint](NOTES-LAYOUT-VALUE-API-MILESTONE.md) retains720. The explicit proof transition requires61 current installed files, nine exact previous images and seven current verifiers, authenticates four overwritten intermediate Vault files and keeps both historical epochs distinct. Past receipts are not rebound. All159 original source-ID/SHA pairs and232 capability IDs remain unchanged. The latest requirement binding refresh covers ${refreshed.length} reviewed local evidence rows.\n\nEncrypted7z support is undergoing independent review. Complete release-bound feature inventories, all missing features and comparative speed, resource use, usability, compatibility and reliability remain active work. This checkpoint is not a completion notification.\n`;
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(studio,milestone),document,{flag:'wx'});
for(const [p,isRoot]of[[path.join(lab,'README.md'),true],[path.join(studio,'README.md'),false]]){let text=fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8');const phrase='The current [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint]';assert.equal(text.split(phrase).length-1,1);text=text.replace(phrase,'The historical [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint]');if(!isRoot){const old='The current record contains **937 passing tests and no skips**, with 737 unchanged source fingerprints.';assert.equal(text.split(old).length-1,1);text=text.replace(old,`The current record contains **${total} passing tests and no skips**, with ${sources} unchanged source fingerprints.`);}text+=`\nThe current [Flow static links and Vault group editing checkpoint](${isRoot?'products/rea-studio/':''}${milestone}) passes **${total} implemented-contract checks, no skips and ${sources} stable source fingerprints**. It adds native static links, exact unedited native text preservation and guarded group Create/Save. Full replacements and comparative acceptance remain under development.\n`;fs.writeFileSync(p,text);}
for(const [i,j]of registries.entries()){j.currentFlowLinksVaultEditMilestone={record:'products/rea-studio/'+milestone,currentCombinedTests:total,currentCombinedSources:sources,installation:'products/rea-studio/'+installationPath,originalSourceIdentitiesPreserved:true,capabilityIdsPreserved:true,fullDocumentationInventoryClosed:false,completeProducts:0};assert.deepEqual(projection(j,registryNames[i]),original[i]);fs.writeFileSync(path.join(studio,'requirements',registryNames[i]),JSON.stringify(j,null,2)+'\n');}
const reqPath=path.join(studio,'requirements/README.md');let req=fs.readFileSync(reqPath,'utf8');req=req.replace('The current [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint]','The historical [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint]');req+=`\nThe current [Flow static links and Vault group editing checkpoint](../${milestone}) refreshes ${refreshed.length} reviewed local implementation evidence rows across the existing251 references. All159 original source identities and232 capability IDs remain unchanged; full feature inventories and comparative acceptance remain open.\n`;fs.writeFileSync(reqPath,req);
const result={schema:'rea-flow-vault-checkpoint-finalization/v1',at:new Date().toISOString(),runName,summary:attempt.summary,sourceFiles:sources,snapshotCount:snapshots.length,preservationSHA256:sha(pb),developmentSHA256:sha(db),metadataBefore,metadataAfter:metadataPaths.map(p=>({path:p,...id(fs.readFileSync(path.join(lab,p)))})),originalSourcePairs:159,capabilityIds:232,completeProducts:0,sourceOnlyCollector:true,appExecutions:0,oldReceiptsRebound:false};fs.writeFileSync(path.join(own,'finalization.json'),JSON.stringify(result,null,2)+'\n',{flag:'wx'});console.log(JSON.stringify(result));
