const doc=`# Search, Save, notebook trash and entry recycling checkpoint\n\nThis is a tested development checkpoint within the accepted ten-product replacement study. Every documented feature and all requested comparative dimensions remain required. Zero products meet full replacement or universal superiority acceptance.\n\n## Installed changes\n\n| Application | Current implemented slice | Focused current checks | Remaining material scope |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Editor | Saved UTF-8 literal cross-file search, bounded traversal/results, revision-bound result navigation, dirty draft retention, late Save publication guards and preconditions captured before queue waits. | 78/78 across15 files | Regex/multiline/whole-word/replace/unsaved search; full editing, encodings, extensions, remote workspaces, original GUI and comparative quality. |\n| Notes | Confirmed recursive local notebook trash/restore, attachment/tag/ID retention, cold persistence and JEX checks, captured action identity and late Save/list guards. | 59/59 | Native confirmation browser acceptance incomplete; visible confirmation panel under separate development. Full sync/shared rules, purge and original application/database/GUI. |\n| Vault | Entry-only native recycling, read-only preview, confirmed restore with supported previous-parent/fallback behavior, tombstones/history/UUID retention and guarded late recycle-list publication. | 79/79 | Group recycling/restore, empty-bin/history settings, broader schemas, full original GUI, security/compatibility/performance acceptance. |\n\nThe combined current suite passed **${dev.summary.pass}/${dev.summary.tests}**, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or unfinished tests. All${sourceCount} captured source files matched before and after the run. [Raw results and exact sources](${prefix}/preservation-manifest.json) bind the run; [current development receipt](results/development-validation.json) records execution. This suite exercises implemented contracts; it does not run a full original acceptance suite or a comparative benchmark. The preceding [686-test public checkpoint](results/milestones/packs-notebooks-history-455ab6c-20261012/snapshot-manifest.json) preserves674 source and23 metadata identities at455ab6c without rebinding any historical receipt.\n\n## Independent corrections and negative results\n\nThe preceding811-test run had810 passes and one outdated permanent-delete assertion. Its source capture contained709 unchanged enrolled files plus an after-only source-census addition from a misplaced metadata verifier; that file was never a test and was later moved to the intended root scripts folder through an explicit source transform. The run is preserved as failed and unaccepted. [Failed run and exact source diagnostic](results/search-trash-recycle-save-failed-20261013/preservation-manifest.json) remains separate. The failed-run diagnostic uses a relative root-verifier label that was one level short; the actual repository path is scripts/verify-editor-save-followup.mjs, preserved in the separate verifier campaign. The corrected Vault HTTP test validates native UUID recycle membership, encrypted export/history/private metadata retention and confirmed permanent purge/tombstones across host-instance restarts; these are in-process host replacements, not OS process restart claims. Its baseline1pass/1fail and corrected2/2 are distinct retained source epochs. The previous138 focused Notes/Vault campaign remains bound to its original105 sources; the later HTTP test update does not rebind those sources.\n\nThe Editor study preserves37→39→42 search epochs, held stale result/draft failures, and the later1024-character path correction. The accepted independent search review passed18 finite cases. Original search engine comparisons retain their prepared-corpus and BOM-mapper limits; no held-out or full editor equivalence claim follows. See [search scope](apps/editor/SEARCH.md) and [search evidence](results/editor-workspace-search-followup/README.md).\n\nA separate seven-case Editor Save review had4pass/3fail: a real disk save committed correctly but its held response could discard newer in-memory text or publish after disposal. A separate three-case direct-call review had2pass/1fail when a shared input object's revision changed while queued; this is an in-process API boundary, not an HTTP exploit. The correction passed41 author checks and14 independent checks (ten overlap). The installed78 corpus is separately executed. Its source-only proposal's16-file prose was corrected to15 by the bound selector/census; the78 total was unchanged. [Exact negative, corrected and independent epochs](results/editor-save-followup/publication-plan/frozen/INTEGRATION.md.snapshot) and [current78 receipt](results/editor-save-followup/current-integration/frozen/validation.json.snapshot) distinguish disk commits, later drafts, synthetic errors with zero commits, and current source bytes.\n\nNotes likewise retains two confirmed initial publication/input faults and subsequent corrected/adjacent campaigns. [Final source-only plan](apps/notes/results/notebook-trash-followup/publication-plan/README.md.snapshot) corrects an earlier prospective73 to59 unique current checks; the old proposal stays immutable. [Current Notes/Vault receipt](results/notes-vault-focused-integration-20261013/frozen/integration-validation.json.snapshot) and [accounting audit](results/notes-vault-focused-integration-20261013/frozen/completion-audit.json.snapshot) bind138 actual tests,105 source fingerprints,34 installed proposal identities and37 authenticated KeePass library processes. They do not credit whole-original applications or GUI sessions.\n\n[Vault recycle scope](apps/vault/RECYCLE.md) preserves its original68 author epoch, initial11 independent groups with three publication failures, corrected38 frontend groups and final7 independent groups. These counts overlap and are not added into one independent corpus. The released default4.0 writer omits PreviousParentGroup; separate explicit4.1/QualityCheck-disabled fixtures preserve it. Production history/XML bytes remain exact.\n\n## Browser acceptance boundary\n\nThe prior Editor browser study passed seven workflows on an earlier124-source correction, with one owned diagnostic expectation failure corrected separately. It does not validate the later path/Save corrections in a browser. Current Notes browser setup created a root/child notebook, saved a note, retained an unsaved draft while refusing notebook organization, and saved it at revision2. Clicking native trash confirmation stalled the browser bridge. No trash reached the server; restore was not exercised. The owned host was forcibly stopped after command identity verification, its source28 and synthetic data stayed exact, and tab closure could not be confirmed. [Full incomplete browser record](results/notes-trash-browser-incomplete-20261013/frozen/browser-validation.json.snapshot) retains all control/cleanup failures. It is not a passed trash workflow. Earlier independent Vault browser evidence is exact and finite.\n\n## Original acquisition and feature discovery\n\nThe official VS Code1.140.0 win32-x64 archive is355,156,158bytes with publisher-matching hashes. Its3,246 regular unpacked files stayed exact; one recorded CLI identity invocation confirms version/commit/architecture. Original GUI and broad behavior checks remain zero. [Acquisition](requirements/vscode-release-acquisition-20261012/README.md) remains separate from Monaco0.57.0 and its different development commit.\n\nThe pinned API declaration study identifies2,909 public syntactic records,2,727 excluding inline signatures,2,850 documented declarations,42 overload groups/102 signatures,109 direct Event annotations and22 direct heritage references (eight external/unresolved). Eight finite parser tests and a separate source-comment scanner pass. [Exact declaration/inventory/source/license evidence](requirements/vscode-extension-api-discovery-20261013/frozen/README.md.snapshot) keeps raw GitLF and releasedCRLF identities separate. This is one declaration file, without semantic typechecking, inherited-member/generic resolution, atomic requirement closure or full workbench discovery. All159 original source fingerprints and232 aggregate capability IDs remain unchanged.\n\n## Comparative results and public preservation\n\nThe fourth Metrics wrapper campaign has147 timing and147 isolated-memory children; its root audit independently authenticates882 raw logs,1,835 numeric PID samples and recomputes441 statistics without new measurements. All-percentile paired median timing is−11.066% but three of seven pairs are slower and timing ranges overlap. Single-p95 lifetime RSS rises from79.395MiB to82.484MiB. Signed negative controls,686 unavailable zero-control percentages and prior regressions remain. Baseline reducer is unchanged and the candidate is unaccepted. [Wrapper observations](results/metrics-wrapper-observations-20261012/README.md) and its prospective diagnostic plan do not imply uniform improvement or another executed experiment.\n\nNotes maps935 source/self-carrier records to920 public inert snapshots and15 copies of one local synthetic TAR/JEX carrier. Vault maps858 records to857 public aliases/471 unique objects (444 new,27 exact reuse) and one local synthetic KDBX carrier. Editor Save maps516 records to174 public source objects (101new,73 reuse). Four Vault screenshots retain original.png aliases despite JPEG headers; exact image bytes are preserved. Local Windows path/username metadata and original source attribution remain explicit. Native vendor executables/full archives/private caches remain local. Root installation collector failures and proposed-source adapter differences are retained; finite scans are not proof of absence of every secret, personal datum or supply-chain risk.\n\nThe next phase continues implementing the missing contracts, beginning with an accessible in-page Notes confirmation and broader release-bound editor compatibility. No completion notification is warranted.\n`;
